QuestGuidance.Register("en",134,{
[4257]="7003783E\n1\tTravel to the Folde Farm\tThe Folde Farm can be found just north of Aldburg. Thane Arcil has asked you to travel to the Folde Farm and warn them of the potential of Orc-attacks.\n2\tTalk to Witgil\tWitgil is somewhere at the Folde Farm. Now that you have arrived at the Folde Farm, you should seek out and speak with Witgil.\n3\tTalk to Arcil\tArcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg to the south of Folde Farm. You have alerted the people at the Folde Farm about the Orc-threat and should now return to Arcil.\n",
[4258]="7003A67C\n1\tTravel to the Folde Farm\tThe Folde Farm can be found just north of Aldburg. Éothain has asked you to travel to the Folde Farm and warn them of the potential of Orc-attacks.\n2\tTalk to Witgil\tWitgil is somewhere at the Folde Farm. Now that you have arrived at the Folde Farm, you should seek out and speak with Witgil.\n3\tTalk to Éothain\tÉothain is near the entrance of Aldburg to the south of Folde Farm. You have alerted the people at the Folde Farm about the Orc-threat and should now return to Éothain.\n",
[4259]="70028CB4\n1\tTalk to Ardwyn at Forthbrond\tArdwyn is at Forthbrond, far to the north of Innoth's camp. Innoth instructed you to bring news of the Orc-caverns to Ardwyn.\n",
[4260]="7003E049\n1\tDefeat invaders in Direnfirel (total: 20)\tTo weaken the resolve of the invaders within Direnfirel, you take it upon yourself to thin their numbers.\n",
[4261]="7003E04B\n1\tDefeat the leader of the enemies within Direnfirel\tQuickbeam has asked you to destroy the leader of the enemy force.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tYou should return to Quickbeam and inform him of your success. Quickbeam can be found at Derndingle.\n",
[4262]="7003E04A\n1\tCollect heirloom tools (total: 8)\tYou should collect the packs of tools left behind in Direnfirel.\n",
[4263]="7001B1D1\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Cirith Nûr (total: 16)\tYou will find Orcs encamped at Cirith Nûr on the west side of the Greenway to the north of the Old Greenway Fort. Andreg asked you to attempt to disrupt the Orcs at their encampment at Cirith Nûr.\n2\tTalk to Andreg at the Old Greenway Fort\tAndreg is at the Old Greenway Fort, south of Cirith Nûr. The Orc-encampment was filled with powerful Orcs, and a cave carved into the cliff face lay within the heart of the camp. You should return to Andreg with your report.\n",
[4264]="700173B9\n1\tDisable the alarms of Fil Gashan ([see journal]/8)\tFil Gashan lies to the south-west of Anazârmekhem. Vagun directed you to attempt to disable the massive alarm bells that the Orcs have placed throughout Fil Gashan. He mentioned that the sentries are good at spotting any who are not their own kind.\n2\tTalk to Vagun at Anazârmekhem\tVagun is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of Fil Gashan. You attempted to disable several of the alarms. While not always successful, as Vagun had warned, the attempt is more important than the success.\n",
[4265]="70058CF2\n1\tFree frost-tusks from hitching posts in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (total: 4)\tFrost-tusks can be found hitched to posts in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. Rádek has asked you to free frost-tusks from their hitching posts in an attempt to sow discord at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.\n2\tTalk to Rádek\tRádek can be found near the gates of Mount Gundabad. You have freed several frost-tusks from their hitching posts at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should return to Rádek.\n",
[4266]="7006BD08\n1\tInvestigate the supplies in Ashâgir (total: 4)\tBâzadur has asked for your help investigating the stolen supplies in Ashâgir. He has suggested inspecting the supplies themselves first to see if you can find out anything.\n2\tReturn to Bâzadur\tReturn to Bâzadur and inform him of what you found while searching the supplies.\n3\tLook for clues near the supply cart\030Look for clues at the nearby shelters\030Look for clues at the nearby rubble\tBâzadur has asked you to look for additional clues around the hideout in Ashâgir.\n4\tReturn to Bâzadur in Ashâgir\tReturn to Bâzadur with the information you have gathered from your investigation in Ashâgir.\n5\tSearch for a hideout near Ningûdu\tBâzadur suggests you investigate a hideout they know of down near Ningûdu, as there may be more clues to the whereabouts of the supplies there.\n6\tInvestigate the corpse\tInvestigate the corpse found at the hideout in Ningûdu, near Ashâgir, for the missing supplies.\n7\tRecover stolen supplies (total: 4)\tRecover the stolen supplies at the hideout in Ningûdu, near Ashâgir.\n8\tReturned the recovered supplies to Bâzadur\tReturn the recovered supplies to Bâzadur in the hideout in the Ashâgir camp.\n",
[4267]="70042910\n1\tTalk to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tBingo is inside his hobbit-hole in the town of Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole. Bingo has to pack for his journey, and has asked you to help him with his final preparations.\n2\tPick up the ball of twine inside Bingo's hobbit-hole\tPoppy Bracegirdle lives across from Bingo's hobbit-hole in Michel Delving. Bingo borrowed a ball of twine from Poppy Bracegirdle and wants you to return it to her before he departs on his journey.\n3\tPick up the teapot inside Bingo's hobbit-hole\tMerrimac Fairbairn lives in the same circle as Bingo in Michel Delving. Bingo borrowed a teapot from Merrimac Fairbairn and wants you to return it to him before he departs on his journey.\n4\tPick up the bucket inside Bingo's hobbit-hole\tMyrtle Boggs lives up a short rise east of Bingo's hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving. Bingo borrowed a bucket from his neighbour Myrtle Boggs and wants you to return it to her before he departs on his journey.\n5\tTalk to Myrtle Boggs outside her hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tMyrtle Boggs is to the east of Bingo's hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving. You have returned the bucket Bingo borrowed from his neighbour Myrtle, and now she wishes to speak with you.\n6\tTalk to Mayor Will Whitfoot outside the Town Hole, in Michel Delving\tMayor Whitfoot is outside the Town Hole, south of Bingo's hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving. Myrtle Boggs does not approve of Bingo's adventure, and has started a petition to have him locked up in the Lockholes instead. She has asked you to see if the mayor has ruled on her petition yet.\n7\tShow Myrtle's petition to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving\tMayor Will Whitfoot has given you Myrtle's petition to give to Bingo, so the hobbit will know what awaits him (and that Myrtle might attempt to lock him up herself!)\n8\tPick up flowers near the statue of Marcho and Blanco, in Michel Delving\tFlowers often sprout up near the statue of Marcho and Blanco, in the centre of Michel Delving. Bingo has asked you to pick some of the flowers that grow near the statue of Marcho and Blanco and give them to Myrtle Boggs in appreciation of being such a good neighbour.\n9\tTalk to Myrtle Boggs\tMyrtle Boggs is standing outside her hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving. You have delivered the flowers to Myrtle, as Bingo requested, and she does not know how to respond.\n10\tTalk to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving\tBingo is inside his house in Michel Delving, just north of the Town Hole. You did as Bingo asked and gave Myrtle Boggs some flowers for her kind thoughts.\n",
[4268]="700400E9\n1\tGather bundles of swords from barrels in Tingobel (total: 4)\030Gather armour pieces from barrels in Tingobel (total: 4)\tBundles of swords and armour pieces can be found in Tingobel in north-eastern Blackroot Vale. Thenidiel has asked you to seek out any remaining weapons and armour pieces in Tingobel in hopes that her people can aid in the defence of Lancrath.\n2\tDeliver the swords and armour pieces to Thenidiel\tThenidiel can be found in Lancrath in south-eastern Blackroot Vale. You have recovered as many weapons and armour pieces as you were able to carry, and should now deliver them to Thenidiel.\n",
[4269]="700399AE\n1\tCollect stolen swords\tDunlendings invading from the west have ransacked a passing cart and stolen numerous blades from Béored's shipment. You should reclaim them.\n2\tCollect stolen swords (total: 8)\tStolen swords can be found in the hands of the nearby Dunlendings. You have come across a wrecked cart that has been partially looted by the nearby Dunlendings. You should defeat them and recover the swords.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have recovered many stolen swords from the nearby Dunlendings.\n",
[4270]="7001927B\n1\tDefeat Orc-smiths (total: 4)\030Destroy weapon-stores (total: 5)\tFanuidhol lies to the north-west of Talan Fanuidhol. Bahanneth wants you to enter Fanuidhol and kill several of the smiths there, as well as to destroy some of the stores of weapons they have forged. The weapons can be found stored towards the back of the camp, further to the north-west.\n2\tTalk to Bahanneth at Talan Fanuidhol\tBahanneth is at Talan Fanuidhol, south-east of Fanuidhol. You should return to Bahanneth with news of your victory.\n",
[4271]="70048CA2\n1\tDestroy Uruk weapons (total: 15)\tUruk weapons can be found in Kala-gijak. You should destroy Uruk weapons.\n2\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found outside Kala-gijak. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[4272]="7000828E\n1\tCollect weapon-chests (total: 5)\030Defeat Hillmen defenders (total: 5)\tThe mysterious Angmarim are outside of the troll-cave in the southern part of Taur Gonwaith, south of Lin Giliath. Baranwen has asked you to collect weapon-chests from the Angmarim and to return them to her so she can destroy the foul weapons.\n2\tTalk to Baranwen\030Collect Weapons Chest (total: 5)\tBaranwen is at Lin Giliath, north-west of Taur Gonwaith. Baranwen is awaiting your return with the Orc-weapons, which she will destroy.\n",
[4273]="7004DA4D\n1\tDeter the discontented (total: 5)\tYou should publically deter discontented Dale-folk who are speaking against the refugees.\n2\tTalk to Gaumar\tYou should return to Gaumar.\n",
[4274]="7004CE2A\n1\tLeave Felegoth\tThranduil has asked you to head to Loeglond. You should leave Felegoth.\n2\tTalk to Galion\tGalion wishes to speak with you inside Felegoth. You should talk to Galion.\n3\tTravel to Loeglond\tLoeglond can be found between Eryn Lasgalen and the Dale-lands. You should travel to Loeglond.\n4\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr.\n",
[4275]="70055004\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discover the Halls of Night\n",
[4276]="70054FEF\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discoverer of Ost Dunhoth.\n",
[4277]="70054FF4\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discoverer of Sâri-surma\n",
[4278]="7002D72C\n1\tCheck on the horse from Combe\tThe horse appears to be staring off into the distance, as if he now knows where he needs to go.\n2\tTalk to Éogar in the Horsefields\t\n",
[4279]="70000192\n1\tUse Roiling Deadly Water (total: 4)\030Collect Phial\tThe pools of Imlad Balchorth are to the west of Myrkworth. The waters in the western parts of Imlad Balchorth are infused with deadly poison, and Thorod wishes to determine the cause.\n2\tBring the phial to Thorod\tThorod is in Myrkworth, east of Imlad Balchorth. Your phials are filled with the deadly water from the roiling pools of Imlad Balchorth.\n",
[4280]="70058E17\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discovery: Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold\n",
[4281]="7005D3FC\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing Discovery: Bâr Nírnaeth, the Houses of Lamentation\n",
